## A Troubling Statistic

As of May 2026, there have been a total of 419 food recalls this year, with Class I recalls - the most serious kind - making up 103 cases. This is a concerning number that underscores the ongoing challenges in ensuring food safety.

## Allergens: The Persistent Culprit

Among the causes of recalls, allergen mislabeling remains a top offender, with 240 cases attributed to undeclared allergens. For example, Silver Moon LP dba Loard's Ice Cream has been involved in several recent recalls due to undeclared allergens like Yellow #5, Milk, and Soy in their ice cream products, including their Banana Ice Cream and Loard's Peppermint Ice Cream. Undeclared allergens pose a serious health risk to consumers who rely on accurate labeling.

## Repeat Offenders

Moonlight Packing Corporation, despite being responsible for 11 recalls this year, shows no signs of significant improvement. Their score of 96 and Grade: F reflects poorly on their practices. Similarly, Albertsons Companies LLC is another firm with a high number of recalls (11) and a concerning failure rate.

## Contaminations and Foreign Objects

Salmonella contamination remains a critical concern, with 112 cases reported this year. California Dairies Inc. had to recall their Low Heat Non-Fat Dried Milk Powder due to potential Salmonella contamination. In contrast, foreign object contamination has resulted in 85 recalls, including the discovery of stainless steel dust and plastic particles in Walker Honey Co's honey products.

## The Bigger Picture

The continued presence of repeat offenders and the high number of recalls highlight systemic issues within the food production industry. While some firms take swift action to rectify mistakes, others seem to falter in implementing adequate control measures.

## Conclusion

Consumers must remain vigilant, and regulators must enforce stricter penalties for non-compliance with safety standards. Food manufacturers bear the responsibility of ensuring their products are safe for consumption, and any lapse in this duty is unacceptable.
